# Served by Cloudflare Workers Assets. `public/` lands flat in `.open-next/assets`,
# so this file ships as `.open-next/assets/_headers`.
#
# Without it Workers Assets serves everything `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`,
# which revalidates content-hashed bundles on every repeat visit. Next fingerprints
# everything under `/_next/static/`, so those are safe to pin forever.
#
# This cannot live in next.config.ts. Workers Assets matches before the worker
# runs, so `headers()` there never sees a request for `/_next/static` or for
# anything out of `public/` — which is why the `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`
# that file declares for `/embed.js` has never actually been sent. Verified
# live: the response carried no CORS header and `max-age=0`.

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The embed loader. A live contract with pages we do not control, so a stale
# copy on somebody else's site is a bug we cannot deploy our way out of — this
# stays short. The CORS header is the one next.config.ts has been promising and
# not delivering; a cross-origin `fetch` or module import of it needs it.
/embed.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

/brand/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/favicon.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/icon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/og.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
